    "text": "I recorded the diagnosis for incident 2 as `platform_scheduler`, with 0.6 confidence.\n\n- **What the incident says:** the Airflow scheduler's last heartbeat was 214 s ago, against a 90 s limit, so nothing is being scheduled.\n- **What the events show:** the `airflow-scheduler` Deployment was scaled from 1 to 0 replicas, and its pod was stopped, on 2026-10-21. No later scale-up or new scheduler pod appears. There are no OOMKilled or error exit codes and no scheduling-capacity events.\n- **Gap:** the scale-down is about 13 days before the incident opened on 2026-11-03. The event feed showed nothing matching that date, so I could not confirm what triggered the outage now. Prometheus is not configured, so I could not check the alert state either.\n\nI also proposed runbook 9 (`09-scheduler-down`) steps for a person. The main one is to scale the Deployment back to one replica, then confirm the heartbeat recovers and queued runs start. If it crashes again, the steps send them to the previous logs and the OOMKilled or database rows of the runbook. Nothing was run.",
